 "tokens_before": 24644, "tokens_after": 24644, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2706c3c9", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 132, 583, 934, 368, 131], "window": [22302, 24701], "confidence": 0.72, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "A directed, time-ordered chain 798->132->583->934->368->131 is supported: the first three hops all occur inside [22302,23501] and the last two inside [23502,24701], with only forward-direction events at each hop. Node 368 had no contact with 131 before 23501 (step_09), so the final hop follows its infection rather than preceding it. The graph is sparse (repeat_ratio 0.004) and neither endpoint is a hub (798: 2 events, 131: 4 events), so volume and popularity do not explain the path. Only caveat: exact timestamps are unobserved, so the <=600 per-hop bound is inferred from the tight two-bin concentration."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure (time-ignored):** 798's 4-hop neighbourhood (step_05) contains a directed path 798\u2192132\u2192583\u2192934\u2192368, and 131's neighbourhood (step_04) shows 368\u2192131. So a candidate directed chain exists: **798 \u2192 132 \u2192 583 \u2192 934 \u2192 368 \u2192 131**.\n\n**Temporal localisation:** Binning activity of the chain nodes into 1200-unit windows (step_06) shows the relevant events are not spread over the whole 9600-unit interval but concentrated in two adjacent bins:\n- [22302, 23501]: exactly 3 events \u2014 verified as 798\u2192132 (step_10), 132\u2192583 (step_11), 583\u2192934 (step_12/step_15)\n- [23502, 24701]: exactly 2 events \u2014 verified as 934\u2192368 (step_13), 368\u2192131 (step_14/step_16)\n\nEvery hop is verified in the *forward* direction only (no reverse events), and the five hops occupy two consecutive short windows in the correct bin order, so the chain is time-respecting end-to-end and each hop's latency is small relative to the 9600-unit interval.\n\n**Confounder controls:** The window has 1775 events over 1375 nodes with repeat_ratio 0.0039 (step_01) \u2014 activity is sparse and non-bursty, so the path is not an artefact of volume. Neither endpoint is a hub: 798 has 2 events / 2 partners and 131 has 4 events / 4 partners (step_02). Intermediate nodes are also low-degree in the pre-arrival window (steps 07\u201309: 132 has 3 partners, 934 has 2, 368 has only 1364 before 23501 \u2014 i.e. 368 had not yet contacted 131), confirming the 368\u2192131 hop occurs *after* 934\u2192368 rather than before it. This rules out \"popular hub / already-connected\" explanations.\n\n**Residual uncertainty:** exact timestamps are not directly observable, so the per-hop gap of \u2264600 is inferred from the two-bin concentration rather than measured exactly; the two cross-bin hops could in principle exceed 600.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2706c3c9\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 132, 583, 934, 368, 131],\n  \"window\": [22302, 24701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A directed, time-ordered chain 798->132->583->934->368->131 is supported: the first three hops all occur inside [22302,23501] and the last two inside [23502,24701], with only forward-direction events at each hop. Node 368 had no contact with 131 before 23501 (step_09), so the final hop follows its infection rather than preceding it. The graph is sparse (repeat_ratio 0.004) and neither endpoint is a hub (798: 2 events, 131: 4 events), so volume and popularity do not explain the path. Only caveat: exact timestamps are unobserved, so the <=600 per-hop bound is inferred from the tight two-bin concentration.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 30860, "total_output_tokens": 11297, "total_tokens": 42157, "total_latency_ms": 150704, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}